---
import { site } from '@app/site';
import Prose from '@app/layouts/Prose.astro';
---

<Prose
  title="Terms of service"
  description="The terms under which Postal is offered."
  updated={site.policyDate}
>
  <p>
    Postal is software you run on your own computer. By using it you agree to these terms. If you do
    not agree, do not use Postal.
  </p>

  <h2>The software</h2>
  <p>
    Postal is a mail client for the terminal. Its source is published at
    <a href={site.repo}>{site.repo.replace('https://', '')}</a>, and the licence in that repository
    governs how you may use, copy and change it.
  </p>

  <h2>Your accounts</h2>
  <p>
    Postal connects to mail accounts you sign in to. You are responsible for those accounts, for the
    mail you send with Postal, and for following the terms of your mail Provider. Postal's developer
    has no access to your accounts or your mail.
  </p>

  <h2>No warranty</h2>
  <p>
    Postal is provided as is, without warranty of any kind, express or implied, including fitness
    for a particular purpose. Mail is important: keep it on your Provider's server, which Postal
    does by default, and do not rely on Postal's Cache as a backup.
  </p>

  <h2>Liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the extent the law allows, Postal's developer is not liable for any loss or damage arising
    from the use of Postal, including lost or undelivered mail.
  </p>

  <h2>Privacy</h2>
  <p>
    The <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a> says what Postal stores and what it connects to.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
  <p>
    A change to these terms is published on this page, with its date at the top. Questions go to
    <span class="address">{site.contact}</span>.
  </p>
</Prose>

<style>
  .address {
    font-family: var(--font-code);
    font-size: 0.9em;
    user-select: all;
  }
</style>
